node_modules/
dist/
# The web console build output is generated by `make web-build` and is fully
# ignored — a deterministic Vite build must never show up as a repo diff. web/dist
# is pure Vite output. internal/app/webui/dist is the go:embed tree: ONLY the
# committed `.gitkeep` sentinel is tracked, so `//go:embed all:dist` always has a
# file and `go build ./...` stays green without a Node build; when no built
# index.html is embedded the handler serves a Go-string placeholder shell. The
# built index.html + hashed assets stay ignored under both dirs.
!internal/app/webui/dist/
internal/app/webui/dist/*
!internal/app/webui/dist/.gitkeep
.DS_Store
*.log
.superpowers/
.dev/
# Playwright (dev-only click-through gate, web/): the runner's report + artifact
# output and its browser cache. Browsers download to the OS cache
# (~/Library/Caches/ms-playwright), never the repo; these dirs are pure run output.
web/test-results/
web/playwright-report/
web/blob-report/
web/playwright/.cache/
web/.last-run.json
# Feeder relay/1 signing keypair + self-signed TLS cert (make-dev-local,
# generated by internal/feeder/signing.LoadOrCreate). Already covered by
# .dev/ above; called out explicitly so key material never gets committed
# even if .dev/ is ever narrowed.
.dev/feeder-keys/
# Feeder relay/1 enrollment registry (make-dev-local, generated by
# internal/feeder/enroll.Server.EnablePersistence) — holds, among other
# things, the feeder's in-process CA private key. Same rationale as
# .dev/feeder-keys/ above.
.dev/feeder-enroll/
# Relay relay/1 operational SQLite (make-dev-local, generated by
# internal/relay/identity.Open) — holds the relay's own enrollment private
# key. Same rationale as .dev/feeder-keys/ above.
.dev/relay-identity/
# App security-model/1 auth state (make-dev-local, generated by
# internal/app/auth.Open + EnsureClaimWindow) — the principal/credential/
# session/grant database plus the first-boot setup code, which is a live claim
# credential until it is redeemed. Same rationale as .dev/feeder-keys/ above.
.dev/feeder-auth/
# Workspace archive destination (make-dev-local, generated by
# internal/app/workspacekey.LoadOrCreate and written by the data-subject export)
# — holds the workspace signing key and data key, plus encrypted archive/1
# containers carrying the whole workspace. Same rationale as .dev/feeder-keys/
# above, and more so: a container IS the workspace.
.dev/feeder-archive/
# Make-dev pack-publisher signing keypair (generated by
# internal/packsig.DevProvision via scripts/examplepack + scripts/packsmoke) —
# the private key the dev example pack is signed with. Same rationale as
# .dev/feeder-keys/ above. The sibling .dev/pack-trust/ anchors document holds
# PUBLIC material only but is machine-local provisioning, not source.
.dev/pack-publisher/
.dev/pack-trust/
# The local dev API key the HTTP probes present (scripts/devkey writes it,
# scripts/devcred reads it). Its home is .dev/feeder-auth/, already ignored
# twice over above — this bare-filename rule additionally catches it wherever
# WAIVEO_DEV_API_KEY_FILE points, including the repo root. It is a LIVE bearer
# credential holding `admin`, so the rule is deliberately broader than the file's
# default location.
dev-api-key

# graphify (local knowledge graph, on-demand dev tooling)
graphify-out/

# Agent-tool scratch: .claude/ holds session state and, under worktrees/, FULL
# checkouts of this repo made for parallel agent runs. A stale one is easy to
# leave behind (a workflow that ends without cleanup), and untracked it is one
# `git add -A` away from committing a second copy of the whole tree into a
# public repo. Ignored rather than tidied by hand for that reason.
.claude/
